      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The study of various myocardial metabolic substrates in basal conditions and in the course of an atrial pacing test in two groups, one control, and the other including angina pectoris in patients with sound coronary arteries, provides the confirmation that the only valid metabolic criterion for acute myocardial ischaemia in man is represented by the decreased extraction or production of lactates. The sugnificance and the specidicity of this parameter is discussed."},
